  "StockRole": "Industrial Mech",
  "YangsThoughts": "The SecuriMax stands as proof of just how badly MaxTech wanted a proper BattleMech to its name, though like other SecurityMechs of its era, its industrial roots simply couldn't compete with the real thing. Its heavy rifles and machine guns had little effect against modern armor, doing real damage only to similarly outdated equipment or vulnerable infantry. It survived for a time on backwater worlds far from modern militaries, but flawed fire control on its missile systems and overall high cost sealed its fate, making it one of MaxTech's shortest lived designs.",
